  "compatibility_assessment": [
    "Source APP_GROUP_ID is provided through each bundle Info.plist; a signed build can remap this configuration to a genuinely provisioned replacement group, if such a group is granted.",
    "KEYCHAIN_SHARED_GROUP is also configurable through Info.plist and native query methods use explicit access groups; any replacement must be an exact group genuinely granted by the selected signed profile.",
    "A main-app-only Foundation fallback to its own sandbox may avoid nil group-container URLs but cannot create shared storage across the eight extension processes.",
    "No foreign keychain access, authentication logic modification, or binary patch has been implemented by this analysis."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Full BuildInfo.keychainSharedGroup propagation through Swift/Rust initialization to each KeychainBinding call has not been independently traced. Field/key semantics and native explicit-group query paths are proven separately.",
    "No conclusions about existing authentication tokens or token contents were drawn; no token values were read.",
    "No runtime startup, authentication persistence, extension behavior, or different-team provisioning was tested.",
    "Foundation direct-call scan covers B/BL targets to the identified Objective-C stub; dynamically generated or indirect call sites may exist.",
    "App Group/Keychain entitlements, extension parent IDs, notification and location-push capabilities must be validated from the actual replacement profiles rather than assumed from the original signing."
